00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:14.470
So my name is Matt.

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.460
I'm a product manager at
Google Cloud Platform.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.960
Today, I'm going to talk about
accelerating investor insight

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.170
with commercial data on GCP.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.080
So as an investor, you
likely need to make decisions

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.750
with facts and not feelings.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:33.770
You have data you know you
need to get insights from

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:35.580
to ultimately make money.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.240
And that's why we're all here.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.110
So as an investor,
I need to discover

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:46.670
untapped opportunities,
understand behavior, what's

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:50.700
going on at the regional
and also the macro level,

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.380
and also anticipate
future trends.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.550
Now, I need to do
all of these things,

00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:00.030
but here are my challenges.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:04.569
Commercial data lives in all
sorts of different silos,

00:01:04.569 --> 00:01:06.380
and each one of them
has a proprietary way

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:07.930
of just serving data to you.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:10.550
So either you connect
to an API or you

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:14.150
connect to an FTP or an
SFTP if you're super fancy,

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:15.742
or someone will ship
you a hard drive.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:18.200
All of these things you've got
to plug into your own system

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.680
and figure out what you're
going to do with it.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.812
And you spend a lot
more effort figuring out

00:01:23.812 --> 00:01:26.270
how to unpack that than actually
analyzing the data itself.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.790
So ultimately, which are yoy?

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:34.710
Are you an investor or
are you a data plumber?

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:37.189
So my personal philosophy is
it shouldn't be this hard.

00:01:37.189 --> 00:01:37.980
How can Cloud help?

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.220
Just to summarize,
Google Cloud Platform

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:46.990
is building a data marketplace.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:52.030
We are hosting commercial
data on Google Cloud Platform,

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:53.540
simplifying distribution.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:55.760
So if you have data in
any of these formats,

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:57.820
we are targeting specific
Google Cloud Products

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:01.084
you distribute them through.

00:02:01.084 --> 00:02:03.000
In terms of access, they
are all authenticated

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.337
through one single mechanism.

00:02:04.337 --> 00:02:06.420
So if you work with five
different data providers,

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.336
you're not authenticating
five different times

00:02:08.336 --> 00:02:12.262
using OAuth2 or passwords
or special HTP headers.

00:02:12.262 --> 00:02:14.220
If you're on Cloud
Platform, you use Cloud IAM.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.428
It's the same authentication
mechanism you're already

00:02:16.428 --> 00:02:17.882
using as a Cloud user.

00:02:17.882 --> 00:02:20.340
The idea here is you can log
in once and access all of them

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.256
all at the same place.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.910
And once it's accessible in the
same place, it's ready for use

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:27.840
by your analysts.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.510
You can use SQL directly
for data in BigQuery.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:33.040
You can use BigQuery itself.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.890
You can export to
Microsoft Excel.

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.870
You can pull data
from Google Sheets.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.619
For the technical
members in the audience,

00:02:38.619 --> 00:02:40.484
you can also use
JDBC/ODBC connectors.

00:02:40.484 --> 00:02:42.150
If you want to throw
a biz layer on top,

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:44.600
BigQuery works out of the box
with Data Studio, Tableau,

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.580
Click, all those
partners up there.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:50.400
Let's say you have
data scientists.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.230
Now you can work with data from
BigQuery Google Cloud Storage.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:55.870
We have a product
called Cloud Data Lab,

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.220
which is a Jupyter notebook.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:59.178
If you're familiar with
scientific or numerical

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:01.570
computing in a Python
library called Pandas,

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:03.250
we have a product for that.

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.830
If you want to start
exploring machine learning

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:08.080
with TensorFlow,
reads from BigQuery

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.530
and also Google Cloud
Storage-- ready to go.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:13.489
And if you have a data
engineering team, great.

00:03:13.489 --> 00:03:15.821
You can work with BigQuery
Google Cloud Storage and also

00:03:15.821 --> 00:03:16.480
Cloud Pub/Sub.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:19.217
Cloud Pub/Sub is our
streaming messaging product.

00:03:19.217 --> 00:03:21.550
From there, you can process
it using data PROC if you're

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.260
familiar with Hadoop
and SPARC, or you

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:26.170
can use Cloud Data Flow, which
unifies both batch and stream

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:28.672
processing.

00:03:28.672 --> 00:03:29.880
Why are we doing all of this?

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:33.990
We want to do this to
accelerate your time to insight.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:36.750
So today, we have a few launch
