00:11:37.219 --> 00:11:38.760
So even visually,
you can see there's

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:40.926
a very interesting correlation,
but you can actually

00:11:40.926 --> 00:11:43.020
get the actual values as well--

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:47.450
a correlation of 0.65
with Newport Mining

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:49.880
and a negative 0.45 with the
Dow Jones Industrial Average.

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:52.540
So you get a feel for not just
is it negative and positive,

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:54.120
but even how much.

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:57.310
Now, really simple
example, right?

00:11:57.310 --> 00:11:59.670
But the point here is that
I never had to download CSV.

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:01.500
I never had to put
in my own database.

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:03.880
I never had to
maintain that solution.

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:05.835
If I wanted to, I
could even go back here

00:12:05.835 --> 00:12:10.800
and say, well, let me just
check against the S&amp;P 500.

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:13.800
Take a different one, run it.

