00:26:08.620 --> 00:26:10.110
That's our bread and butter.

00:26:10.110 --> 00:26:12.240
We've been doing it
for over 125 years.

00:26:12.240 --> 00:26:14.700
We are the Wall Street
Journal, we are Market Watch,

00:26:14.700 --> 00:26:17.440
we are Barrons, we
are Financial News.

00:26:17.440 --> 00:26:19.080
So we have a wealth of content.

00:26:19.080 --> 00:26:23.280
And not only that, we also
have a very rich taxonomy.

00:26:23.280 --> 00:26:26.160
So we have a robust
data strategy team

00:26:26.160 --> 00:26:29.250
that actually curates
and updates the taxonomy

00:26:29.250 --> 00:26:31.682
that we apply on top of our
content, which makes now

00:26:31.682 --> 00:26:34.140
our content even more valuable
in terms of how you might be

00:26:34.140 --> 00:26:38.550
able to leverage it within
your firm to deliver insights

00:26:38.550 --> 00:26:40.560
around your
particular use cases.

00:26:40.560 --> 00:26:42.820
We have over 30,000
sources of content.

00:26:42.820 --> 00:26:44.910
So beyond just the
content that we create,

00:26:44.910 --> 00:26:47.940
we actually ingest all
sorts of other publications,

00:26:47.940 --> 00:26:49.980
premium news across the globe.

00:26:49.980 --> 00:26:53.100
And we actually then apply
this taxonomy on top of it

00:26:53.100 --> 00:26:55.090
in over 28 different languages.

00:26:55.090 --> 00:26:58.170
We have over 19.5 million public
and private companies that

00:26:58.170 --> 00:27:00.070
are encoded in this taxonomy.

00:27:00.070 --> 00:27:02.100
We have over 1,500
new subjects that

00:27:02.100 --> 00:27:05.670
are encoded in this
taxonomy, over 2,400 regions,

00:27:05.670 --> 00:27:07.530
and we have over 1.2
billion documents

00:27:07.530 --> 00:27:09.210
and growing in our archive.

00:27:09.210 --> 00:27:12.090
So it's a wealth of
content that now people

00:27:12.090 --> 00:27:14.550
are starting to
leverage in terms

00:27:14.550 --> 00:27:16.800
of whether it's quant
firms, whether it's

00:27:16.800 --> 00:27:19.935
wealth managers, whether
it's financial advisors--

00:27:19.935 --> 00:27:21.810
in terms of being able
to take that and build

00:27:21.810 --> 00:27:24.450
predictive models now
that can help drive

00:27:24.450 --> 00:27:27.850
how they do their investments.

00:27:27.850 --> 00:27:33.300
So we're very excited to do a
little soft launch of Dow Jones

00:27:33.300 --> 00:27:34.230
DNA.

00:27:34.230 --> 00:27:36.390
DNA stands for Data
News and Analytics.

00:27:36.390 --> 00:27:39.840
It's a new platform that we've
developed completely on Google.

00:27:39.840 --> 00:27:41.736
It's leveraging a lot
of Google's big data

00:27:41.736 --> 00:27:43.110
technologies-- a
lot of the stuff

00:27:43.110 --> 00:27:44.850
that Matt talked about earlier.

00:27:44.850 --> 00:27:47.520
We're leveraging Dataflow
and Dataproc and Google Cloud

00:27:47.520 --> 00:27:51.640
Storage and BigQuery to
make our wealth of content

00:27:51.640 --> 00:27:54.411
now available to customers in a
much more accessible way, that

00:27:54.411 --> 00:27:56.910
can really help them innovate
and push the envelope in terms

00:27:56.910 --> 00:27:59.790
of how they could leverage
content within their business.

00:27:59.790 --> 00:28:02.977
We have three main ways of being
able to access this content.

00:28:02.977 --> 00:28:04.560
We have what's called
Snapshots, to be

00:28:04.560 --> 00:28:06.290
able to get large archives.

00:28:06.290 --> 00:28:08.890
In the past, when customers
came to us and said,

00:28:08.890 --> 00:28:11.790
hey, we'd like to get a year's
worth of your news archive,

00:28:11.790 --> 00:28:13.680
it would take us
weeks to deliver it,

00:28:13.680 --> 00:28:17.550
and we'd deliver it
via FTP and CSV files.

00:28:17.550 --> 00:28:19.587
And it was really
difficult for a customer

00:28:19.587 --> 00:28:21.420
to be able to really
take advantage of that.

00:28:21.420 --> 00:28:23.760
Now, with things
like Google Cloud,

00:28:23.760 --> 00:28:27.630
we can deliver a 30-year
archive, a 100-year archive,

00:28:27.630 --> 00:28:29.280
in literally an hour--

00:28:29.280 --> 00:28:31.380
30 minutes to an hour.

00:28:31.380 --> 00:28:34.144
So it's really changing the way
customers can take advantage

00:28:34.144 --> 00:28:36.060
of our content, whether
it's to do backtesting

00:28:36.060 --> 00:28:38.340
to build predictive models,
whether it's to leverage

00:28:38.340 --> 00:28:41.700
or to do specific research
around very specific use cases,

00:28:41.700 --> 00:28:43.265
and so on.

00:28:43.265 --> 00:28:44.640
Another way we're
delivering this

00:28:44.640 --> 00:28:46.181
is through what
we're calling Stream.

00:28:46.181 --> 00:28:48.030
We're actually using
Google Cloud Pub/Sub

00:28:48.030 --> 00:28:51.180
to be able to deliver our
news content in near real time

00:28:51.180 --> 00:28:52.080
to customers.

00:28:52.080 --> 00:28:54.030
So imagine now
you're going to be

00:28:54.030 --> 00:28:56.610
able to go in, leverage a
30-year archive of news,

00:28:56.610 --> 00:28:58.560
build a predictive
model, and then apply

00:28:58.560 --> 00:29:00.830
that predictive model
now on a stream,

00:29:00.830 --> 00:29:04.467
and now essentially delivering
to you real time insights that

00:29:04.467 --> 00:29:06.300
actually is actionable
that you can actually

00:29:06.300 --> 00:29:10.410
take and start automating
within your organization.

00:29:10.410 --> 00:29:12.090
And then we also have
a rich set of APIs

00:29:12.090 --> 00:29:15.330
that we're building out on
top of the cloud as well,

00:29:15.330 --> 00:29:18.360
to be able to do much more
of the request response

00:29:18.360 --> 00:29:20.990
type of use cases, where you
might want specific data.

00:29:20.990 --> 00:29:23.140
Because we also have a
wealth of company data,

00:29:23.140 --> 00:29:24.820
for example, and so forth.

00:29:24.820 --> 00:29:27.180
So you may want to
understand what's

00:29:27.180 --> 00:29:30.810
going on with a specific company
in terms of their profile

00:29:30.810 --> 00:29:33.450
and you may want to correlate
that with news content

00:29:33.450 --> 00:29:34.350
and so forth.

00:29:34.350 --> 00:29:37.620
We have search APIs as
well to really dive deeper

00:29:37.620 --> 00:29:40.170
into our news content
if you're looking

00:29:40.170 --> 00:29:43.480
for very specific
pieces of information.

00:29:43.480 --> 00:29:46.969
And we're building a
very accessible ecosystem

00:29:46.969 --> 00:29:48.510
around this as well
to make it easier

00:29:48.510 --> 00:29:52.170
for customers to be able to
leverage this new platform.

00:29:52.170 --> 00:29:53.940
We're launching a
new developer portal,

00:29:53.940 --> 00:29:56.065
we're building out a customer
solutions engineering

00:29:56.065 --> 00:29:58.650
team ourselves, and we're
really building on our partner

00:29:58.650 --> 00:30:00.720
ecosystem with
partners like Google

00:30:00.720 --> 00:30:03.446
in terms of making our data
more available to our customers.

00:30:06.780 --> 00:30:09.240
And these are some of the
very cool things that people

00:30:09.240 --> 00:30:12.060
are starting to do now
with this new platform

00:30:12.060 --> 00:30:15.900
and with this new accessibility
to premium news content.

00:30:15.900 --> 00:30:18.000
Internally, we had
a little code-athon,

00:30:18.000 --> 00:30:20.520
and literally in
a matter of days,

00:30:20.520 --> 00:30:23.682
we were able to build
these cool little assets.

00:30:23.682 --> 00:30:25.890
We were actually leveraging
Google's natural language

00:30:25.890 --> 00:30:28.290
processing API on
top of this platform

00:30:28.290 --> 00:30:32.550
to do things like geo encoding
and sentiment analysis

00:30:32.550 --> 00:30:34.970
and so forth on top of the data.

00:30:34.970 --> 00:30:36.360
We were doing things--

00:30:36.360 --> 00:30:39.090
leveraging our streams
to show real time

00:30:39.090 --> 00:30:42.480
trending topics, trending
companies, trending sectors,

00:30:42.480 --> 00:30:44.770
things of that nature that
you could start doing.

00:30:44.770 --> 00:30:46.710
And then we also built
out a little demo

00:30:46.710 --> 00:30:49.080
to show where you
can type in a company

00:30:49.080 --> 00:30:51.210
and you can see the news
volume about that company

00:30:51.210 --> 00:30:52.960
over a timeline.

00:30:52.960 --> 00:30:54.760
And all of this
now is very easy,

00:30:54.760 --> 00:30:56.790
even for you guys
to do internally

00:30:56.790 --> 00:30:58.117
within your business.

00:30:58.117 --> 00:30:59.700
And these are some
of the other things

00:30:59.700 --> 00:31:03.300
that people are, for example,
leveraging our content for.

00:31:03.300 --> 00:31:05.350
Imagine, being able
to go in-- again,

00:31:05.350 --> 00:31:07.290
because we have a
very robust taxonomy--

00:31:07.290 --> 00:31:11.360
to be able to quickly understand
the impact of various trade

00:31:11.360 --> 00:31:14.880
