00:33:48.620 --> 00:33:50.420
So how many of you,
when you're meeting

00:33:50.420 --> 00:33:51.650
a stranger for the
first time, you

00:33:51.650 --> 00:33:53.024
have to try to
think of something

00:33:53.024 --> 00:33:54.104
to talk to them about?

00:33:54.104 --> 00:33:56.270
Well, usually one of the
first things you talk about

00:33:56.270 --> 00:33:58.670
is either television
or the weather,

00:33:58.670 --> 00:34:00.920
because weather affects so
much of our everyday lives.

00:34:00.920 --> 00:34:03.260
It affects how
many steps we take,

00:34:03.260 --> 00:34:05.936
it affects what music we
listen to, it affects--

00:34:05.936 --> 00:34:07.310
and of course,
most importantly--

00:34:07.310 --> 00:34:10.190
what consumers buy, which
is what investors really

00:34:10.190 --> 00:34:12.110
care about.

00:34:12.110 --> 00:34:13.940
But there are some
challenges in order

00:34:13.940 --> 00:34:15.800
to predict human behavior.

00:34:15.800 --> 00:34:17.510
It requires a large
amount of data

00:34:17.510 --> 00:34:19.670
and a large amount
of technology.

00:34:19.670 --> 00:34:23.210
And we know the environment has
a strong impact on consumers,

00:34:23.210 --> 00:34:26.570
but again, predicting human
behavior is very difficult.

00:34:26.570 --> 00:34:28.760
I'm a sociologist by
training, and we usually say,

00:34:28.760 --> 00:34:31.040
if it was easy, it
would be rocket science.

00:34:31.040 --> 00:34:33.080
So every piece of
information you

00:34:33.080 --> 00:34:35.960
have to help you predict to
what consumers are going to do

00:34:35.960 --> 00:34:38.090
will help you
improve your model.

00:34:38.090 --> 00:34:40.880
So the environment has a
huge impact on consumers

00:34:40.880 --> 00:34:45.060
and most importantly, weather
has an effect as well.

00:34:45.060 --> 00:34:47.239
So our solution--
we want to make sure

00:34:47.239 --> 00:34:50.300
that you have access to
highly accurate and reliable

00:34:50.300 --> 00:34:52.139
historical weather data.

00:34:52.139 --> 00:34:54.260
So if you have bad
data coming in,

00:34:54.260 --> 00:34:56.600
no matter how good
your modeling is,

00:34:56.600 --> 00:35:00.170
how advanced your machine
learning techniques are,

00:35:00.170 --> 00:35:03.200
if the data behind it
is bad, then the output

00:35:03.200 --> 00:35:04.700
is going to be bad as well.

00:35:04.700 --> 00:35:07.640
We've had several of our
clients come to us saying, oh,

00:35:07.640 --> 00:35:09.950
we heard about this
other data source.

00:35:09.950 --> 00:35:12.980
The website looked great and
we did a little bit of digging,

00:35:12.980 --> 00:35:15.680
and we found out it was
some guy working out

00:35:15.680 --> 00:35:18.630
of his mom's basement
playing X-Box half the time.

00:35:18.630 --> 00:35:20.990
So you want to make sure
you do your due diligence

00:35:20.990 --> 00:35:23.910
when you're looking for
these data sources to ingest.

00:35:23.910 --> 00:35:27.320
So having a good source like
Google with reliable partners

00:35:27.320 --> 00:35:28.820
is very important.

00:35:28.820 --> 00:35:30.650
And so having this
weather information

00:35:30.650 --> 00:35:33.830
allows you to unlock these
aspects of human behavior

00:35:33.830 --> 00:35:37.350
and to uncover new insights.

00:35:37.350 --> 00:35:41.570
So keeping this short and sweet,
